{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"overcorrection in batch adjustment overcorrection in batch adjustment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment.md","fileName":"Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 20:21\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Batch Effects and Latent Factor Adjustment]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Batch Effects and Latent Factor Adjustment","Biological Signal","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"overcorrection in batch adjustment overcorrection in batch adjustment","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment.md","fileName":"Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment","heading":"Overcorrection in Batch Adjustment","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Overcorrection in batch adjustment occurs when a correction removes genuine [[Biological Signal]] together with unwanted technical variation. Blindly deleting leading principal components is risky because an outcome correlated with batch may contribute to those same high-variance directions.\n\nThe source demonstrates overcorrection when removing dominant components eliminates expected sex-chromosome findings and produces a shortage of small p-values. Adjustment must model the protected outcome explicitly rather than assuming every dominant component is nuisanc